---

<section class="research page-gutter" id="research" aria-labelledby="research-title">
  <div class="research__head">
    <h2 class="research__title" id="research-title">Research</h2>
    <p class="research__intro">
      How language shaped by generative AI enters decisions that are hard to
      reverse, and what the data work behind that question actually looks like.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="research__body">
    <div class="research__study">
      <p class="research__study-title">
        Examining AI-Generated Content in Equity Crowdfunding: Implications for
        Investor Evaluation and Trust
      </p>
      <p class="research__study-meta">
        With Ruiyang Wang. Department of Computer Science,&nbsp;Cal Poly Pomona.
      </p>
      <p class="research__study-meta">
        Presented at the RSCA Conference 2026.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="research__notes">
      <section class="research__note" aria-labelledby="research-questions">
        <h3 class="research__note-title" id="research-questions">Questions</h3>
        <p class="research__note-text">
          Does AI-generated or AI-characteristic language change how investors
          evaluate a venture and how much they trust it? Does sustainability
          messaging behave differently when it is asserted during the campaign
          than when it is adopted after the raise?
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="research__note" aria-labelledby="research-methods">
        <h3 class="research__note-title" id="research-methods">Methods</h3>
        <p class="research__note-text">
          A mixed-method comparative design. The pre-AI baseline uses
          Crowdcube campaigns from 2017 to 2018, tracked to long-run outcomes and
          analysed with logistic regression, which is reported as odds ratios.
          A contemporary Republic dataset records daily funding and investor
          counts along with campaign updates and discussion posts, collected by
          hand because the platform does not permit automated scraping.
          Computational text analysis compares AI-characteristic terminology,
          linguistic patterns, and syntactic structures in campaign materials.
          Investor surveys and founder interviews are designed and pending
          institutional review board approval.
        </p>
        <p class="research__note-text">
          Separately, an enrichment audit covered 219 campaigns across eight
          fields, 1,752 field checks in total, with every applied correction
          backed by a source URL and an identity check.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="research__note" aria-labelledby="research-findings">
        <h3 class="research__note-title" id="research-findings">
          Preliminary findings
        </h3>
        <p class="research__note-text">
          From the pilot analysis of the pre-AI Crowdcube baseline. These are
          associations in the data, not causal effects, and the textual and
          survey phases are still in progress.
        </p>
        <ul class="research__findings">
          <li>
            International orientation during the campaign was associated with a
            higher probability of long-run survival.
          </li>
          <li>
            Sustainability positioning during the campaign was associated with a
            lower probability of long-run survival and a higher probability of
            bankruptcy or insolvency. Becoming sustainable after the raise was
            strongly associated with higher long-run survival.
          </li>
          <li>
            Post-raise sustainability pointed toward lower bankruptcy or
            insolvency risk, but the evidence was statistically inconclusive.
            Acquisition outcomes were recorded, though the number of acquired
            ventures was too small to support reliable interpretation.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="research__note" aria-labelledby="research-status">
        <h3 class="research__note-title" id="research-status">Status</h3>
        <p class="research__note-text">
          Presented as a research poster at the RSCA Conference 2026. This is an
          ongoing study and a conference presentation, not a published paper, and
          the textual and survey phases are still in progress.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
